# No browser right-click in Command Center

Command Center must feel like a persistent desktop application, not a web page.

## Required

- `installContextMenuGuard()` (`src/lib/contextMenuGuard.ts`) stays installed in `main.tsx`. It prevents the browser context menu on every right-click.
- A right-click on something without an app menu does nothing.
- Right-click only opens the app's own menus (for example the Rules/Skills row menu). Those handlers keep working because the guard only calls `preventDefault`, never `stopPropagation`.
- Text fields and editors (`input`, `textarea`, `select`, `[contenteditable]`) keep the browser menu for copy and paste.

## Forbidden

- Removing or bypassing the guard, or adding page-level code that re-enables the browser menu outside text fields.

